      ],
      "sampled_audio_range_seconds": [
        2.109899301,
        31.399653003
      ],
      "observation": "Full health shows clear edges. The first hit displays 60 HP, a restrained red perimeter and a left-side directional cue. The roughly 14-second checkpoint still shows 60. Consecutive frames 435-437 show 63, then 44 with a renewed stronger edge. The later pre-delay checkpoint still shows 44. The player, centre and essential HUD remain readable."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Changed maximum and explicit restoration",
      "viewed_frames": [
        "Media/frame_00833.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00834.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00847.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00848.jpg"
      ],
      "sampled_audio_range_seconds": [
        32.639352702,
        33.241773602
      ],
      "observation": "The configured 200-HP portion shows 47 then 58 with a short red health bar and visible missing-health perimeter. The next frame after explicit restoration shows 100, a full teal bar and clear edges. The configured maximum and exact recovery rate come from the separate runtime records, not a maximum-health label in these images."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Three HUD motifs, timers and refill",
      "viewed_frames": [
        "Media/frame_00849.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00853.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00862.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00863.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00867.jpg"
      ],
      "sampled_audio_range_seconds": [
        33.283528902,
        33.9902924
      ],
      "observation": "The coral skull and gold x2 each have readable notification text and compact timer rows. Max Ammo shows a distinct teal crate icon; ammunition changes from 6/56 to 7/84 with no third timed row. The later Insta-Kill notification is refreshed. Rapid fixture collection leaves no useful uncollected skull or x2 world-model view in this sample."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Actual collected-effect pistol kill",
      "viewed_frames": [
        "Media/frame_00881.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00882.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00883.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00884.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00894.jpg"
      ],
      "sampled_audio_range_seconds": [
        34.516884603,
        34.980171502
      ],
      "observation": "Consecutive 881-884 show the standing target, actual muzzle flash/tracer, gold hit feedback, ammunition 7 to 6, and the points total 0 to 220 while both timed-effect rows remain visible. Frame 894 shows the target folded locally with small blood marks and a restrained +220 gain beside the points total. The popup is inside the viewport; a read-only colour-pixel measurement places its warm glyphs at x35-77, y718-735. Target health and the exact body-kill award are separately asserted by runtime records."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Pause, recovery and early world crate",
      "viewed_frames": [
        "Media/frame_00895.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00910.jpg",
        "Media/frame_00968.jpg",
        "Media/frame_01312.jpg",
        "Media/frame_01345.jpg",
        "Media/frame_01375.jpg"
      ],
      "sampled_audio_range_seconds": [
        35.012218401,
        52.891140703
      ],
      "observation": "Both pause images show 29-second timers, 80 health and the same 1-kill/220-point summary. After resume, the early uncollected crate is bright teal/cyan with dark face/lid and cartridge markings, and a small visible teal floor glow. Frame 968 is about 2.12 gameplay seconds after this fixture drop was created, well before warning/fade. It stays visibly distinct in later ordinary-life samples. Health remains 80 at the later pre-delay sample, then shows 92 and finally 100 with clear edges. This resolves the earlier S1 dark-crate observation in the sampled S3 location."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Effect expiry, world expiry and death cleanup",
      "viewed_frames": [
        "Media/frame_01673.jpg",
        "Media/frame_01689.jpg",
        "Media/frame_01717.jpg",
        "Media/frame_01726.jpg",
        "Media/frame_01734.jpg"
      ],
      "sampled_audio_range_seconds": [
        64.170979202,
        66.409329001
      ],
      "observation": "The Double Points row is absent while Insta-Kill reads 1 second, then both are absent while the crate remains. A later sample shows the crate gone. Game Over is legible with 0 health and no active timer rows or red injury perimeter. The final 3-kill/460-point tally includes the actual pistol kill plus two explicit award fixtures; it is not three naturally played kills."
    }
